<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Shaddad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 955</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad ibn Shaddad was the founder of the Shaddadid dynasty, a Kurdish family that rose as the Sallarid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> declined. In 951 he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, though he could not hold it, and he died in 955. His sons established the family at Ganja in Arran, where the Shaddadids ruled the lands between the Kura and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Araxes</a> until the late 11th century.</p></div>
